2026-07-29T16:55:03.6866927Z Skipping the duckdb test suite.
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6867098Z 
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6867380Z The duckdb tests exercise DuckDB's bundled C++ engine and are deliberately
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6867926Z NOT run on CRAN. They run automatically on GitHub Actions (including
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6868444Z r-universe). This keeps check time and resource usage on CRAN within
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6869130Z acceptable limits and helps release duckdb in a predictable and controlled
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6869509Z manner.
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6869619Z 
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6870249Z This is intentional, not an oversight. duckdb has an extensive test suite
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6870872Z that runs continuously in our own CI; see <https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-r>.
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6871199Z 
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6871482Z To run the test suite locally, set the environment variable before checking:
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6872014Z   Sys.setenv(DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS = "true")    # from within R, or
2026-07-29T16:55:03.6872503Z   DUCKDB_R_RUN_TESTS=true R CMD check ...      # from the shell
